<%# The search trigger, shared by the nav and the footer so the two can't drift — a copy that
    lost the pointerenter/focus actions would silently give up intent-prefetch on that surface.
    A button, not an <a href="#">: search needs JS, so there's no destination to fall back to.
    `wrapper_class` (required local) is the list-item class of the menu it sits in. %>
<li class="<%= wrapper_class %>">
  <button type="button" data-controller="search" data-action="click->search#open pointerenter->search#preload focus->search#preload">Search</button>
</li>
